I am standing in front of building number twelve.
I find Eva's name and ring the doorbell.
The door opens, and I walk up the stairs.
Eva is standing in the doorway and smiles broadly.
"Hi Maya, welcome!" she says and gives me a hug.
"Thanks for the invitation," I answer.
I step into her apartment.
It is very cozy and full of colorful art.
I give her the yellow tulips.
I hope that she does not already have a vase with flowers on the table.
Eva looks at the flowers and looks very happy.
"How beautiful they are!" she exclaims.
"I love yellow flowers."
I feel that I often understand her creative taste.
"I will find a vase for them right away," Eva says.
"You should just go into the living room," she continues.
I take off my shoes and go in there.
The dining table is beautifully set with fine glasses.
I intend to relax and enjoy the evening.
